@prefix ex: <http://example.org/kg-study#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Question 1.1
ex:CatMemoryManagement ex:hasQuestion ex:Q1_1 .
ex:Q1_1 a ex:Question ;
    ex:questionText "How does Python manage memory under the hood (Ref Count vs GC)?" ;
    ex:answerText "Primary memory management uses reference counting. Cyclic references are handled via Generational GC." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/memory.html> .

# Question 2.1
ex:CatDecorators ex:hasQuestion ex:Q2_1 .
ex:Q2_1 a ex:Question ;
    ex:questionText "How do Decorators work under the hood, and how do you preserve metadata?" ;
    ex:answerText "Decorators wrap callables. Preserving metadata requires @functools.wraps(func)." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.wraps> .

# Question 3.1
ex:CatGIL ex:hasQuestion ex:Q3_1 .
ex:Q3_1 a ex:Question ;
    ex:questionText "What is the GIL and how do you choose between asyncio, threading, and multiprocessing?" ;
    ex:answerText "GIL prevents multi-thread bytecode execution. Asyncio handles I/O, multiprocessing handles CPU tasks." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/init.html#thread-state-and-the-global-interpreter-lock> .

# Question 4.1
ex:CatSMTSolvers ex:hasQuestion ex:Q4_1 .
ex:Q4_1 a ex:Question ;
    ex:questionText "How does Z3 SMT solver differ from an OWL reasoner?" ;
    ex:answerText "OWL operates under OWA for classification. Z3 uses CWA for first-order logic constraints." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3/wiki> .